{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-confinement-operator-selection","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:confinement-operator-selection","kind":"proposition","title":"Confinement operator selection via topological Brunnian minimality","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-frobenius-gram-matrix"],"tags":["confinement","borromean","brunnian","topological-selection","frobenius-dual","gram-matrix","operator-selection","beta-decay"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.confinement_operator_selection","text":"confinement-operator-selection.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:confinement-operator-selection\"></a><p><em>Among three-strand braid closures, the Borromean braid <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{B}_3 = (\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1})^3</code> is selected as the confinement operator by the topological principle of crossing-minimal Brunnian nontriviality. Its closure is the crossing-minimal nontrivial Brunnian three-link. The Frobenius Gram and Markov-trace data act as a consistency check on this topologically selected operator, rather than its selector.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/confinement-operator-selection.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"14.2.3","page":"b/prop-confinement-operator-selection","qa":{"counts":{"pass":89,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":14,"unknown":0,"stale":77},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Confinement.confinement_operator_selection","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Confinement/confinement_operator_selection.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
